<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Technical Discussions and Proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Useful Lemma</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our main theoretical result is based on the use of the following Lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> a positive function. The solution of the weighted likelihood objective of the form:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\argmax_{\pi}\left\{\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi_{0}(\cdot|x)}\left[g(x,c,y)\log\pi(c,y|x)\right]\right\}\," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\argmax_{\pi}\left\{\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi_{0}(\cdot|x)}\left[g(x,c,y)\log\pi(c,y|x)\right]\right\}\,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">can be computed analytically and is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall x,(y,c)\,,\pi^{\star}(c,y|x)\propto g(x,c,y)\pi_{0}(c,y|x)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall x,(y,c)\,,\pi^{\star}(c,y|x)\propto g(x,c,y)\pi_{0}(c,y|x)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this Lemma below for completeness. The objective is a constrained optimization problem, that can be solved by Lagrange multipliers. For a fixed input <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we want to maximize:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi)=\sum_{c,y}\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)\log\pi(c,y|x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi)=\sum_{c,y}\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)\log\pi(c,y|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">subject to the normalization constraint:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x)=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x)=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Setting up the Lagrangian:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda)=\sum_{c,y}\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)\log\pi(c,y|x)-\lambda\left(\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x)-1\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda)=\sum_{c,y}\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)\log\pi(c,y|x)-\lambda\left(\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x)-1\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the partial derivative with respect to <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(c,y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(c,y|x)</annotation></semantics></math> and setting it to zero:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(c,y|x)}=\frac{\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)}{\pi(c,y|x)}-\lambda=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(c,y|x)}=\frac{\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)}{\pi(c,y|x)}-\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Solving for <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(c,y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(c,y|x)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(c,y|x)=\frac{\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)}{\lambda}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(c,y|x)=\frac{\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)}{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the normalization constraint <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{c,y}\frac{\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)}{\lambda}=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{c,y}\frac{\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)}{\lambda}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\sum_{c,y}\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\sum_{c,y}\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting back:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}(c,y|x)=\frac{\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)}{\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi_{0}(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x)g(x,c^{\prime},y^{\prime})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}(c,y|x)=\frac{\pi_{0}(c,y|x)g(x,c,y)}{\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi_{0}(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x)g(x,c^{\prime},y^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}(c,y|x)\propto g(x,c,y)\pi_{0}(c,y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}(c,y|x)\propto g(x,c,y)\pi_{0}(c,y|x)</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Analytical Solution of <span id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We remind the reader of the <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> algorithm below:</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span><span id="algorithm2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">R</span>easoning with <span id="algorithm2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">o</span>ffline <span id="algorithm2.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">i</span>terative <span id="algorithm2.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">R</span>einforcement <span id="algorithm2.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L</span>earning (<span id="algorithm2.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span>)</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.16" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.16.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input</span>: Policy <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, transforms <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{m})_{m\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{m})_{m\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, prompt dataset <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\{x_{i}\}_{i\in[n]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\{x_{i}\}_{i\in[n]}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of candidates <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.16.2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.16.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.16.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize</span>: <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}=\pi_{\theta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}=\pi_{\theta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.16.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.16.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.16.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.16.3.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.16.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.16.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.16.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            Construct offline dataset <math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.16.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.16.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            Using <math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we approximate and solve the weighted log-likelihood objective

<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmax_{\theta}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi_{m-1}(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[g_{m}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1}))\log\pi_{\theta}(c,y|x_{i})\right]\right\}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmax_{\theta}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi_{m-1}(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[g_{m}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1}))\log\pi_{\theta}(c,y|x_{i})\right]\right\}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
Set <math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{m}\leftarrow\pi_{\theta_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{m}\leftarrow\pi_{\theta_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm2.16.6" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> leverages a set <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{m})_{m\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{m})_{m\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> of increasing reward transform <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{m}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}\,,\forall m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{m}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}\,,\forall m</annotation></semantics></math> that implicitly control the reward influence. At iteration <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, the analytical solution of Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 3 Self Supervised Reasoning with Iterative Offline Reinforcement Learning ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> takes the form:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall(c,y),x_{i}\,,\quad\pi_{m}(c,y|x_{i})\propto\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall(c,y),x_{i}\,,\quad\pi_{m}(c,y|x_{i})\propto\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this result by induction on the iteration number <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Base Case (<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>):<span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
At iteration <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we solve:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{1}=\argmax_{\theta}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi_{0}(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[g_{1}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{0}))\log\pi_{\theta}(c,y|x_{i})\right]\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{1}=\argmax_{\theta}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi_{0}(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[g_{1}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{0}))\log\pi_{\theta}(c,y|x_{i})\right]\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">As the optimization problem is decomposable, we can look at each <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> independently. Let <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be a prompt from <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the previous Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.1 Useful Lemma ‣ Appendix A Technical Discussions and Proofs ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, the analytical solution is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{1}(c,y|x_{i})\propto g_{1}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{0}))\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{1}(c,y|x_{i})\propto g_{1}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{0}))\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">This matches our claimed form with <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{1}(c,y|x_{i})\propto\left(\prod_{j=1}^{1}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})=g_{1}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{0}))\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{1}(c,y|x_{i})\propto\left(\prod_{j=1}^{1}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})=g_{1}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{0}))\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inductive Step:<span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Assume the claim holds for some iteration <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{m-1}(c,y|x_{i})\propto\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m-1}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{m-1}(c,y|x_{i})\propto\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m-1}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">At iteration <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we solve:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{m}=\argmax_{\theta}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi_{m-1}(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[g_{m}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1}))\log\pi_{\theta}(c,y|x_{i})\right]\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{m}=\argmax_{\theta}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi_{m-1}(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[g_{m}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1}))\log\pi_{\theta}(c,y|x_{i})\right]\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the previous lemma, the analytical solution is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{m}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{m}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto g_{m}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1}))\pi_{m-1}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto g_{m}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1}))\pi_{m-1}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting the inductive hypothesis:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{m}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{m}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto g_{m}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1}))\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m-1}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto g_{m}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1}))\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m-1}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m}g_{j}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{j-1}))\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the induction and proves the claimed form.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span><span id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> solves the <span id="A1.SS3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> objective and beyond</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> objective provides an offline, iterative alternative to the recently proposed <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> algorithm. We recall that <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> optimizes the KL regularized expected reward:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi)\right]-\beta\operatorname{KL}(\pi,\pi_{0}|x_{i})\right\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim\pi(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi)\right]-\beta\operatorname{KL}(\pi,\pi_{0}|x_{i})\right\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This optimization problem differs from the classical regularized objective as the individual rewards depend themselves on the current policy we are optimizing. We can connect <span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> and <span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> with the following proposition:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 3.1. ‣ 3 Self Supervised Reasoning with Iterative Offline Reinforcement Learning ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us focus on the <span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> objective. As the problem is decomposable over prompts, the optimal policy <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> can be recovered for each <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then optimize:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{i}(\pi)=\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x_{i})\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi)-\beta\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x_{i})\log\frac{\pi(c,y|x_{i})}{\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{i}(\pi)=\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x_{i})\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi)-\beta\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x_{i})\log\frac{\pi(c,y|x_{i})}{\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the method of Lagrange multipliers with the constraint <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x_{i})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x_{i})=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=J_{i}(\pi)-\lambda_{i}\left(\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x_{i})-1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=J_{i}(\pi)-\lambda_{i}\left(\sum_{c,y}\pi(c,y|x_{i})-1\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the functional derivative with respect to <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(c,y|x_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(c,y|x_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi)+\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x_{i})\frac{\partial\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi)}{\partial\pi(c,y|x_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi)+\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x_{i})\frac{\partial\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi)}{\partial\pi(c,y|x_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\beta\log\frac{\pi(c,y|x_{i})}{\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})}-\beta-\lambda_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\beta\log\frac{\pi(c,y|x_{i})}{\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})}-\beta-\lambda_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The key challenge is the second term, which captures how changing <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> affects all other rewards <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> through the policy dependence.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the optimal policy <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, rearranging:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})}{\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})}{\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi^{\star})+\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi^{\star}(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x_{i})\frac{\partial\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi^{\star})}{\partial\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})}-\beta-\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi^{\star})+\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi^{\star}(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x_{i})\frac{\partial\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi^{\star})}{\partial\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})}-\beta-\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the exponential:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi^{\star})+\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi^{\star}(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x_{i})\frac{\partial\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi^{\star})}{\partial\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})}-\beta-\lambda_{i}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi^{\star})+\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi^{\star}(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x_{i})\frac{\partial\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi^{\star})}{\partial\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})}-\beta-\lambda_{i}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the normalization constraint to determine <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first-order conditions become:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi^{\star})+\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi^{\star}(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x_{i})\frac{\partial\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi^{\star})}{\partial\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})}\right]\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi^{\star})+\sum_{c^{\prime},y^{\prime}}\pi^{\star}(c^{\prime},y^{\prime}|x_{i})\frac{\partial\tilde{r}_{k}(y^{\prime},x_{i},\pi^{\star})}{\partial\pi^{\star}(c,y|x_{i})}\right]\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, as the rewards are indicator functions, which is discontinuous, their derivative is null almost surely. This allows us to set all the rewards partial derivative to <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, obtaining a fixed point equation that <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall(c,y)\,,\pi^{\star}(c,y|x)\propto\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi^{\star})\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall(c,y)\,,\pi^{\star}(c,y|x)\propto\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi^{\star})\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL<span id="A1.SS3.p10.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> targets this solution by solving Equation <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Preliminaries ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. However, obtaining this solution can also be conducted by solving the fixed point equation directly. The fixed point solution can be solved by iterating over <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> the following:
</span></span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Collect a dataset <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Update <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{m}\propto\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi_{m-1})\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{m}\propto\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi_{m-1})\right)\pi_{0}(c,y|x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">until you reach convergence of the policy <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. The update step can be solved by optimization, and can be implemented by the following Algorithm:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span>Fixed Point Approach</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm3.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm3.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input</span>: Policy <math id="algorithm3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, prompt dataset <math id="algorithm3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\{x_{i}\}_{i\in[n]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\{x_{i}\}_{i\in[n]}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of candidates <math id="algorithm3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm3.4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize</span> <math id="algorithm3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm3.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm3.4.3.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm3.4.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
              Construct offline dataset <math id="algorithm3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algorithm3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
              Set <math id="algorithm3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{m-1}(y,x_{i})=\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi_{m-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{m-1}(y,x_{i})=\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\pi_{m-2})</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="algorithm3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math> else <math id="algorithm3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{m-1}(y,x_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{m-1}(y,x_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
              Using <math id="algorithm3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we approximate and solve the weighted log-likelihood objective

<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmax_{\pi}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{m-1}(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1})-b_{m-1}(y,x_{i}))\right)\log\pi_{\theta}(c,y|x_{i})\right]\right\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmax_{\pi}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{m-1}(\cdot|x_{i})}\left[\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x_{i},\theta_{m-1})-b_{m-1}(y,x_{i}))\right)\log\pi_{\theta}(c,y|x_{i})\right]\right\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>

</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.7" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">This algorithm is exactly Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 3 Self Supervised Reasoning with Iterative Offline Reinforcement Learning ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with the particular choice of <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> to be:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{m}(y,x)=\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x,\pi_{m-1})-b_{m}(x,y)\right)\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{m}(y,x)=\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x,\pi_{m-1})-b_{m}(x,y)\right)\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{m-1}(y,x)=\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x,\pi_{m-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{m-1}(y,x)=\tilde{r}_{k}(y,x,\pi_{m-2})</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math> else <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{m-1}(y,x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{m-1}(y,x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A1.SS3.p11.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> can exactly target the optimal solution of <span id="A1.SS3.p11.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> with the choice of <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> in Equation <a href="#A1.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 RoiRL solves the TTRL objective and beyond ‣ Appendix A Technical Discussions and Proofs ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. This ends the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Extended Empirical Results</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Experimental Details</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.1 </span>Implementation Details</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compared three training methods using the same hyperparameters. In all experiments, we generate <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=10</annotation></semantics></math> candidates for each problem and then train on these candidates using the chosen reward function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>. We used our custom <code id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">WeightedSFTTrainer</code> to implement learning with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\beta}:x\rightarrow\exp(x/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\beta}:x\rightarrow\exp(x/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> and used standard <code id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">SFTTrainer</code> to implement <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{I}:x\rightarrow x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{I}:x\rightarrow x</annotation></semantics></math>, as it is equivalent to using supervised finetuning on candidates with answers corresponding to majority vote. We will refer to the proccess of generating candidates and training on them as 1 round of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span>. In both methods, after generating candidates, we train for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> epochs during every round. We trained all methods for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math> rounds, with early stopping if <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{maj}_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">maj</mtext><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{maj}_{10}</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy on the train dataset did not improve for more than <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> rounds. We take the round with the best performance on train, when reporting the final accuracies.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All hyper-parameters were set to their default values in <code id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">SFTTrainer</code>, the only exception being the reduction of the learning rate from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\cdot 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\cdot 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> for Llama-3.2 with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> because higher values result in overfitting. We implemented <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> with Huggingface <code id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">GRPOTrainer</code> and used its default parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In our experiments, we compare one round of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> with one epoch of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> as both require the same number of generations, namely, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kn</annotation></semantics></math>. However, note that <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> is computationally more demanding and thus requires more time per epoch. More details of the computational advantages of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> over <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> are discussed in <a href="#A2.SS1.SSS3" title="B.1.3 Computational advantages of RoiRL ‣ B.1 Experimental Details ‣ Appendix B Extended Empirical Results ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.2 </span>Evaluation</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To obtain the majority vote, we generate <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> answers from the model using temperature sampling with a temperature equal to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. The maximum number of new tokens is set to 1024. We then extract the answers from the generated solution, find the one that has the most occurrences, and choose it as our majority vote answer. If two answers have equal number of occurrences, we pick one of them randomly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To extract the answer, we find the first occurrences of <code id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed{}</code> in the generated solution and consider everything that was put inside the brackets as the final answer. Qwen2.5-Math automatically puts the final answer inside <code id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed{}</code> and to ensure the same behavior from the other two models, we add a phrase “<code id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">Put your answer in \boxed{}</code>” to the prompt.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since the same answer can be written in multiple ways (for example, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) we used <code id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">sympy</code> to parse latex and then compared the answers as sympy objects. In case of parsing or comparison errors or timeouts, we fallback and compared the answers as strings.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.3 </span>Computational advantages of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span></h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> method has several computational advantages over <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span>. Firstly, we strictly separate the generation and the training phases and this allows better batching during generation. More precisely, we can generate answers to multiple questions in a single batch, unlike online RL algorithms such as <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span>. Secondly, our reward method does not require storing logits, so we can use larger batch size during generation compared to <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span>. Unlike GRPO, our method does not use a reference model to compute the reward, further reducing its computational cost. And finally, using a sparse reward function (e.g., <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>) in <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> can significantly speed up the training phase, especially in the early stages, when the majority answers are sparse. With all these advantages combined, we achieve performance more than <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 2.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 2.5</annotation></semantics></math> times faster per 1 round of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> compared to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> epoch of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span>. The exact time evaluations for <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> and <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> with sparse (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>) and dense (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>) reward functions are presented in Table <a href="#A2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ B.1.3 Computational advantages of RoiRL ‣ B.1 Experimental Details ‣ Appendix B Extended Empirical Results ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments were conducted on a Google Cloud Platform (GCP) instance with a single NVIDIA A100 (80Gb VRAM), 12 vCPUs and 170 GB RAM running on Debian GNU/Linux 11 (bullseye). <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> and <span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span> methods were implemented using the Hugging Face Transformers library v4.52.4, TRL v0.18.2 and PyTorch v2.7.1 with CUDA 12.4.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="A2.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Time per round comparison</span></figcaption>
<table id="A2.T2.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T2.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Method</th>
<th id="A2.T2.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Time per round</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T2.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span>, <math id="A2.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> (sparse reward)</th>
<td id="A2.T2.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">6552.5s</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A2.T2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span>, <math id="A2.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> (dense reward)</th>
<td id="A2.T2.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">8883.5s</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.T2.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span></th>
<td id="A2.T2.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">17019.25s</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Detailed Results and Discussions</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ B.2 Detailed Results and Discussions ‣ Appendix B Extended Empirical Results ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <a href="#A2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ B.2 Detailed Results and Discussions ‣ Appendix B Extended Empirical Results ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ B.2 Detailed Results and Discussions ‣ Appendix B Extended Empirical Results ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> illustrate the training curves for Qwen2.5-Math-1.5B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, Phi-4-mini-reasoning-4B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, and Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> trained with <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> and <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span>. The greedy decoding baseline and the <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{maj}_{128}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">maj</mtext><mn>128</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{maj}_{128}</annotation></semantics></math> baseline are represented by horizontal lines.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> consistently improves the accuracy on the MATH500-train dataset and successfully generalizes on a holdout MATH500-test dataset, AMC and AIME datasets. Note that unlike supervised finetuning, <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> does not require ground-truth labels even on the train dataset, so this is a self-improvement process. Compared to <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span>, <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> demonstrates faster convergence with the same number of training rounds and less computations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> improves not only the sampling accuracy (dotted lines), but also the <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{maj}_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">maj</mtext><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{maj}_{10}</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy (solid lines). Moreover, for Qwen-2.5 and Phi-4, after several epochs the sampling accuracy exceeds the initial <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{maj}_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">maj</mtext><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{maj}_{10}</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy. This demonstrates how <span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> does not just distill the majority vote performance into the base model, but improves the general ability to solve mathematical problems.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.02892v1/images/qwen_2.5/qwen_all_plots.png" id="A2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/340;" width="476" height="340" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="A2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Training curves for Qwen-2.5-Math</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.02892v1/images/phi4/phi4_all_plots.png" id="A2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/340;" width="476" height="340" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="A2.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Training curves for Phi-4</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.02892v1/images/llama_3b/llama3b_all_plots.png" id="A2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/340;" width="476" height="340" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="A2.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Training curves for Llama-3.2</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ B.2 Detailed Results and Discussions ‣ Appendix B Extended Empirical Results ‣ RoiRL: Efficient, Self-Supervised Reasoning with Offline Iterative Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> illustrates the evolution of the average entropy during training for Qwen2.5 on MATH500-Train and Test. When using the <span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span>, entropy rapidly decreases to almost zero. However, for <span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TTRL</span>, the entropy stays relatively high during the whole training process. This can explain faster convergence of <span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> during our experiments. In addition, the fast reduction of the entropy to zero with <span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RoiRL</span> raises a natural question of applying more regularization, implicitly by reducing the learning rate or using alternative reward functions, which may be the subject of further research.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.02892v1/images/entropies/qwen_entropy_comparison_train_test.png" id="A2.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/232;" width="476" height="232" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A2.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Entropies for Qwen2.5 on MATH500</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
